 20	// Postgres migrations apply on boot and are a hard gate. There is no separate
 21	// migration container and no manual step, and two instances starting at once
 22	// cannot both apply. A file that fails throws here, before anything is served:
 23	// an instance running against a schema it could not finish applying would look
 24	// healthy until the first read of a column nobody created. Authentication and
 25	// acceptance both depend on this store, so nothing can usefully start without
 26	// it.
 27	const migrations = await runMigrations(config.databaseUrl);
